{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak to all the congregation of the children of Israel.</b> This teaches that this passage was proclaimed in assembly, like the Ten Commandments. And why? Because all the commandments are included in it: there — 'I am' (אנכי), and here — 'I am YHWH your Elohim'; there — 'You shall not have' (לא יהיה לך), and here — 'Do not turn to the idols' (אל תפנו אל האלילים); there — 'You shall not take [the name]' (לא תשא), and here — 'Do not swear by My name' (לא תשבעו בשמי); there — 'Remember' (זכור), and here — 'Keep My Sabbaths' (את שבתותי תשמורו); there — 'Honor your father and your mother' (כבד את אביך ואת אמך), and here — 'A man, his mother and his father' (איש אמו ואביו); there — 'You shall not murder' (לא תרצח), and here — 'Do not stand by the blood of your fellow' (לא תעמוד על דם רעך); there — 'You shall not commit adultery' (לא תנאף), and here — 'The adulterer and the adulteress shall be put to death' (מות יומת הנואף והנואפת); there — 'You shall not steal' (לא תגנוב), and here — 'You shall not steal' (לא תגנובו); there — 'You shall not bear false witness' (לא תענה ברעך), and here — 'You shall not go about as a talebearer' (לא תלך רכיל בעמך); there — 'You shall not covet' (לא תחמוד), and here — 'You shall not oppress' (לא תעשוק). And this passage is juxtaposed to the passage of forbidden relations, so that they not think that solely through observing the forbidden relations will they endure in the land, for there are also other commandments upon which their enduring in the land depends." "<b>You shall be holy.</b> From all that I have warned you about in the adjacent context."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:26.526834655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}